    "family_reading": {
        "text": "MoonshotAI Kimi is an open weights family, with all 7 versions publishing weights, and 5 of the 7 supporting reasoning. Context windows run from 131072 to 1048576 tokens, and the line accepts image, text and video input while returning text only. The newest version, Kimi K3, offers the largest context at 1048576 tokens and the longest output at 943718 tokens, priced at $0.72 per million input and $13 output. Other versions sit near $0.45 to $0.95 input and $2.25 to $4 output, so K3 is the costly option. The facts suggest the family suits long document, image and video understanding with reasoning, and self hosting given open weights. Limits are the text only output, the higher cost of the largest context version, and the fact that two earlier versions lack reasoning support.",
